# AskAlert Project Rules

AskAlert is an agentic marketplace where an AI agent finds vendors or buyers, negotiates, and recommends the best options. Launch market: Lekki, Lagos, Nigeria. Tagline: Ask. Alert. Delivered.

## Stack

- TypeScript (strict)
- pnpm workspaces
- Turborepo
- Next.js App Router
- Tailwind CSS
- Vitest
- Zod

## Layout

- `apps/web`
- `apps/admin`
- `packages/ui`
- `packages/category-engine`
- `packages/payments`
- `packages/config`

## Money

- Always use integers in minor units (kobo). Never floats.
- Every amount carries a currency code.
- Format Naira with `Intl.NumberFormat('en-NG')`.

## Design

- Use design tokens only. Never hard-coded hex values inside components.
- Navy text on orange buttons.
- Never white small text on orange.
- Minimum touch target 44px.
- Mobile-first.
- Support light and dark mode.

## Content

- Plain English.
- Short sentences.
- Friendly and clear.

## Quality

- No `any`.
- No unused code.
- Every package has tests.
- Run `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, and `pnpm test` before finishing any task.

## Security

- No secrets in code.
- Keep an `.env.example`.
- Validate all external input with Zod.

## Process

- Small commits.
- Explain what changed.
- Ask before adding a new dependency.
